MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_001: Goliath! What were you thinking?!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_002: Whoa, coming on strong. Take it easy, kid. Gonna\nmake my head hurt.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_003: That bag of nuts I dropped finally made its way\nback to me.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_004: Oh, glad it got there. You here to thank me?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_005: No! Why'd you hand it off to a soldier to deliver\nto me? That's a lot of extra steps.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_006: Not really getting what the problem is.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_007: I get the feeling you've been avoiding me for\nsome reason.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_008: If you got a problem with me, say so. Don't lumber\naround like nothing's wrong.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_009: So loud! Can you go away?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_010: Don't dodge the question. Answer me!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_011: See, this is why I don't like kids.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_012: They see the big, mean guy up close, and they\nstart screaming.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_013: You think I'd act like those babies? Get real.\nYou don't scare me at all.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_014: Hehehe. Sure, kid. At least you got more guts than\nmost of 'em.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_015: Usually they turn tail by now.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_016: But you're just like the rest. You think I'm scary too.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_017: Hmph! Keep telling yourself that. It's just an excuse\nto avoid me.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_018: And I'm gonna prove you wrong by sticking to you\nlike glue.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_019: Huh? Why do you wanna do that?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_020: Don't think you're gonna weasel outta this. I'll show\nyou I ain't a scaredy-cat.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_C_021: Oh, man. I got a feeling this is going to get\nREAL annoying.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_001: Alright, you made your point! Can you stop following\nme now?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_002: I told you I'd stick close to prove I ain't scared of you.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_003: I haven't cried or screamed once in all the time we've\nbeen walking around. So what's the problem?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_004: Ugh. I wanted to do something fun. Can't do ANY\nfun stuff with a kid around.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_005: Hey... Why don't you buy yourself some sweets at\nthat store? I'll give you something to pay.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_006: For real? That's so nice of you!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_007: But after you eat them, you go home. OK?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_008: Whatever you say, man. Thanks! I'll be right back.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_009: Why's it taking so long? Not that hard to buy\na little candy.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_010: Guess I'll check on her. Ugh. Kids!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_011: I told you, I have the money. I'm gonna pay for\nit—honest I will.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_012: Oh yeah? C'mon. We know who you are.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_013: You were a big-name pickpocket back in Breston.\nThat was you, right?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_014: I dunno what you're talking about.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_015: Don't pretend. Our orphan gang knows everything!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_016: Just show us your skills and you can join our crew.\nOne job at that store, and you're in.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_017: Hey, what's the holdup?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_018: The Butcher?! What's he doing here?!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_019: Catchin' up with my friend. You rug rats got\nsomething to say to her?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_020: N-nope! Sorry!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_021: That was amazing! Didja see those brats run?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_022: Your mean-mugging was just in time.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_023: Yeah...thanks. Guess I'm glad I could help.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_024: And that I didn't hit any of 'em. Then it would've\nended with a lot worse than scared kids.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_025: Yeah, a big guy like you would've clobbered 'em.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_026: I'm not making a joke. When I was back home,\nI almost killed a kid once.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_027: Never meant to hurt anyone—but nobody believed\nme when I said it.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_028: Oh. Uh, sorry about that. It must've been rough.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_029: But don't you worry about me—I'm no softie.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_030: You are pretty scrappy. I bet you'd be a tough one to\ntake out.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_031: Yup. But I'm still gonna hang around you. There's\ntoo much of an upside not to!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_B_032: Huh?! Hey—I ain't your bodyguard!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_001: Uh-oh, comin' from behind. That's not good.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_002: Hyyyah!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_003: You OK, Goliath? I got you some breathing room.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_004: Thanks, Loretta! Now, let's hit 'em hard.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_005: That oughta do it. Close call, huh?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_006: You saved me! You really toughened up, y'know?\nReally got my back now.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_007: Aww, c'mon. You don't gotta flatter me.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_008: But I do feel like I can hold my own next to you\nnowadays.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_009: Yep. You went from a loud little brat to my trusty\nbattle buddy!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_010: Hehehe. Oh yeah. I was kind of a thorn in your\nside in those days.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_011: Hey, you wanna take a walk around with me like\nwe used to?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_012: I ain't the little snot I was. I'm a full-grown woman!\nNot so bad being seen with me now, right?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_013: Weird saying that about yourself. Besides, what are\nyou talking about?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_014: What, I gotta spell it out for you? I'm a looker!\nA catch!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_015: I don't really see it.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_016: I mean, if I had to really think about it, you are taller.\nGot pretty eyes...
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_017: Hang on! What am I thinking? Am I losing it?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_018: Hello? Goliath?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_019: Are you too dazzled for words?
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_020: No! I don't know what you're talking about.
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_021: Well, I'll count it as a win anyway. Score one for me!
MID_SE_Gol_Lor_A_022: Eh... You might be older, but I guess you aren't any\nless of a brat.